 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Find a dry day with no wind. On the ground, rub the dry kindling with an axe or machete until it sparks. They do, though they're bit fizzy. An old steel wash tub works too. About the size of a haystack, so it doesn't get out of control. Mix the water and tea bag just before you put the pot on fire. Let cool completely, then put it in plastic bag and store it in the cupboard.",
